; The one module a plugin compiled from an external module's OCaml
; implementation links against: the table its generated registration
; code fills in, and the interpreter in `pyk` reads (see
; docs/libraries.md, "How the interpreter reaches an OCaml
; implementation"). A library of its own, and unwrapped, so that a
; plugin compiled outside this build names it `Pyk_plugin` and finds its
; .cmi beside the executable. It depends on the standard library alone.

(library
 (name pyk_plugin)
 (wrapped false)
 (flags
  (:standard -warn-error -a)))
